Z||000000||johnt671||08-12-2001||05:22 PM||||I just went to the junkyard and pulled a throttle body w/ a tps on it to try and end my floating idle.  Put it on my 84 with a new gasket on the manifold. Also put a used map sensor in.  The idle still varies.  I have a new isc on it, no vacum leaks, t b is tight on the manifold, the egr valve is tight w/ a new gasket, and I just quit.  I should be happy as the car runs great excpt for this, but that just makes it more frustrating.  Found my egr passages under the t b were compleatly cloesd by carbon and cleaned them out.  Car runs a bit better with the different t b excpt the idle. ||||reg||8
