Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||08-12-2001||06:43 PM||||Do you get any codes?<BR>What is it idling at?<P>I have the same problem with my 85.<BR>I have replaced the following.<BR>IAC<BR>O2<BR>Bad fuel pump<BR>fuel injector<BR>EGR<BR>Distributor<P>I am looking at replacing the coil.<BR>My Idle is around 1500 warm but will not idle when cold.<BR>Once it is warm it will idle under load at around 900.<BR>I can live with it like that for now till I can afford a rebuild. I think after 16 years the motor is just too far gone to tweak it back to a steady idle.<P>Best of luck <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://web.tampabay.rr.com/jakedragon" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/logo.gif">   </A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||johnt671||08-12-2001||07:04 PM||||That may be my problem, too.  205000 miles will do that.  I just put a MSD coil and 6A system in, with fresh plugs and accell wire a new used erg and temp sensor.  Mine starts fine and high idles, but when it goes into closed loop the idle floats between 600 and 950 rpms.  I was getting a 24 code when the car was still and Haynes said to ignore this, but metioned adjusting the TPS.  since I replaced the TB and other stuff I don't get a code.  I may just drill out the plug and try speeding the idle up a hair to try and smooth it out.  Oxygen sensor is about a month ouy Bosh unit.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 08-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||btoth||08-12-2001||08:38 PM||||Did you change the cap and rotor, too, while you were doing everything else to it?<P>Did you check the gap on the plugs?<P>Did you check the timing?<P>Just some suggestions.||||reg||1
